note as DEP_diagram_36b_qa_lab_ext
  Connects to the base qa_lab diagram via:
  qa_lab.test_suites, qa_lab.test_environments, qa_lab.test_runs (last_run_id),
  qa_lab.test_cases, qa_lab.test_case_results, iam.users, directory.tenants,
  terminology.catalog_concepts. test_schedules trigger test_runs on cron.
end note

note as HARDENING_diagram_36b_qa_lab_ext
  REC 3.4 — HARDENING (QA Lab)
  - test_schedules: UNIQUE(suite_id, environment_id, code); concurrency_policy controls
    overlapping runs; next_run_at derived from cron_expression (recompute).
  - test_defects: UNIQUE(tenant_id, defect_number); dedupe by
    (test_case_id, failure_signature_hash); occurrences_count is derived (REC 3.3).
end note

note as VALUE_SETS_diagram_36b_qa_lab_ext
  VALUE SETS
  trigger->vs_test_trigger{manual,scheduled,ci_push,ci_pr,webhook};
  concurrency_policy->vs_concurrency_policy{allow,forbid,queue};
  defect_type->vs_defect_type{bug,flaky,regression,environment,data};
  defect status->vs_defect_status{open,triaged,in_progress,resolved,wont_fix};
  notify_channel->vs_notify_channel{email,slack,webhook,none}.
end note


